From: Jesse Casco <jesse.casco@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gdsc: remove genpds on unregister and error paths

gdsc_init() calls pm_genpd_init(), which adds the domain to the global
gpd_list, but nothing ever called pm_genpd_remove(). The struct gdsc (and
its embedded generic_pm_domain) lives in the clock controller module's
.data, so after rmmod the global list retains a node pointing into freed
module memory.

The unload itself is silent and returns 0. The failure surfaces on the
next modprobe:

  list_add corruption. next->prev should be prev (...), but was 0
  WARNING: lib/list_debug.c:29 __list_add_valid_or_report
   pm_genpd_init+0x4c0/0x4d0
   gdsc_register+0x274/0x6f0
   qcom_cc_really_probe+0x48c/0x590
  debugfs: 'gpu_cc_cx_gdsc' already exists in 'pm_genpd'

and any subsequent read of /sys/kernel/debug/pm_genpd/pm_genpd_summary
oopses in summary_show() while walking the dead node.

Add gdsc_pm_domain_remove() and call it from gdsc_unregister() after the
subdomains and the provider are gone (pm_genpd_remove() rejects a domain
that still has subdomains or devices attached).

The same leak exists on two gdsc_register() error paths: a gdsc_init()
failure returned without unwinding the domains already initialised, and
the return of of_genpd_add_provider_onecell() was passed through
unchecked. Both now unwind.

Reproduced and fixed on an ASUS Zenbook A16 (Snapdragon X2 / glymur) with
gpucc-glymur built as a module; six consecutive rmmod/modprobe cycles are
now clean. Note CONFIG_QCOM_GDSC is bool, so gdsc.c is built in and this
requires a kernel rebuild rather than a module swap.

Signed-off-by: Jesse Casco <jesse.casco@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/gdsc.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/gdsc.c
index 95aa07120..d5bf1351a 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gdsc.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gdsc.c
@@ -566,6 +566,18 @@ static void gdsc_pm_subdomain_remove(struct gdsc_desc *desc, size_t num)
 	}
 }
 
+static void gdsc_pm_domain_remove(struct gdsc_desc *desc, size_t num)
+{
+	struct gdsc **scs = desc->scs;
+	int i;
+
+	for (i = num - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
+		if (!scs[i])
+			continue;
+		pm_genpd_remove(&scs[i]->pd);
+	}
+}
+
 int gdsc_register(struct gdsc_desc *desc,
 		  struct reset_controller_dev *rcdev, struct regmap *regmap)
 {
@@ -606,7 +618,7 @@ int gdsc_register(struct gdsc_desc *desc,
 		scs[i]->rcdev = rcdev;
 		ret = gdsc_init(scs[i]);
 		if (ret)
-			return ret;
+			goto err_pm_domain_remove;
 		data->domains[i] = &scs[i]->pd;
 	}
 
@@ -625,10 +637,20 @@ int gdsc_register(struct gdsc_desc *desc,
 			goto err_pm_subdomain_remove;
 	}
 
-	return of_genpd_add_provider_onecell(dev->of_node, data);
+	ret = of_genpd_add_provider_onecell(dev->of_node, data);
+	if (ret)
+		goto err_pm_subdomain_remove;
+
+	return 0;
 
 err_pm_subdomain_remove:
 	gdsc_pm_subdomain_remove(desc, i);
+	gdsc_pm_domain_remove(desc, num);
+
+	return ret;
+
+err_pm_domain_remove:
+	gdsc_pm_domain_remove(desc, i);
 
 	return ret;
 }
@@ -640,6 +662,7 @@ void gdsc_unregister(struct gdsc_desc *desc)
 
 	gdsc_pm_subdomain_remove(desc, num);
 	of_genpd_del_provider(dev->of_node);
+	gdsc_pm_domain_remove(desc, num);
 }
 
 /*
